A move is a copy beside the source and a delete of the source,
so what was derived from the source goes to the source's parent, or becomes a root,
and a revoke through the moved capability no longer takes it.
The tree stays whole and the move grants nothing new; only its place is lost,
but for an Untyped: the pools made of it go to its parent, and the moved one overlaps them.
The replay's prologue moves two made Untypeds, so the overlap shows before any record runs;
move-loses-place is the mutant the move check is held to.

